==Battleground==
*5 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 16.67~30 seconds<sup>500f~900f</sup>.
*5 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 23.33~43.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,300f</sup>.
*3 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 1.67~3 seconds<sup>50f~90f</sup>.
*5 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 1~1.67 seconds<sup>30f~50f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
**10 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
**20 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 2~3 seconds<sup>60f~90f</sup>.
**5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~3 seconds<sup>30f~90f</sup>.
**3 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**5 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**3 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The stage starts out with some weak peons to allow you to build money, send out meatshields and [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]]/[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]. Some Brollows will come out, but your Manic Flying Cats/Cameraman Cats should be able to hold them off. Alternatively, send out only [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cats]], who (if deployed one at a time) will allow you to stall long enough for max money. Then it's mainly a matter of spamming all your other [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] (preferably [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]]), including some [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] and/or heavy hitters.

==Trivia==
*The term ''Oiesōdō'' (お家騒動) in Trouble at the Mansion's Japanese name, Bukeyashiki Oiesōdō (武家屋敷お家騒動, "Family Trouble at the Samurai Mansion"), literally means "family trouble" or "domestic trouble", but could also refer to an internal squabble (over headship rights) in a daimyo family during the Edo period of Japan.

